; DRAFT replacement for gcc/config/c33/c33.opt.
;
; NOT yet in the build.  The tree currently carries the renamed V850 option
; set, whose TARGET_* masks are referenced throughout c33.cc and c33.h.
; Swapping this in means renaming those masks at the same time; see
; "Next steps" in README.md.
;
; Option names are dictated by the existing toolchain: samo-lib passes
; -mc33pe -mlong-calls, and mini-libc additionally passes -medda32.

HeaderInclude
config/c33/c33-opts.h

Enum
Name(c33_core) Type(enum c33_core) UnknownError(unknown C33 core %qs)

EnumValue
Enum(c33_core) String(c33) Value(C33_CORE_STD)

EnumValue
Enum(c33_core) String(c33adv) Value(C33_CORE_ADV)

EnumValue
Enum(c33_core) String(c33pe) Value(C33_CORE_PE)

mc33
Target RejectNegative Alias(mcore=, c33)
Generate code for the standard C33 core.

mc33adv
Target RejectNegative Alias(mcore=, c33adv)
Generate code for the C33 ADV core.

mc33pe
Target RejectNegative Alias(mcore=, c33pe)
Generate code for the C33 PE core.

mcore=
Target RejectNegative Joined Enum(c33_core) Var(c33_core) Init(C33_CORE_STD)
Select the C33 core variant.

mlong-calls
Target Mask(LONG_CALLS)
Use xcall rather than scall, so callees may be anywhere in the 32-bit address space.

medda32
Target Mask(EXT_32)
Do not use the %r15-relative default data area; address globals absolutely.

memcpy
Target Mask(MEMCPY)
Call memcpy for block moves rather than expanding them inline.
